G1798.d:
ἐνύπν-ιον, τό, 
(ὕπνος) thing seen in sleep, in apposition with ὄνειρος, θεῖός μοι ἐνύπνιον ἦλθεν ὄνειρος a dream from the gods, a vision in sleep, came to me, [Refs 8th c.BC+].; ἐ. παιδός the vision of a boy, [Refs 1st c.BC+] 'to feast with the Barmecide', [Refs 5th c.BC+]; compare{ἐνύπνιος} 
2 after [Refs 8th c.BC+], dream, ὄψις ἐνυπνίου the vision of a dream, [Refs 5th c.BC+] a mere dream, and ὄνειρος a significant, prophetic one; but the distinction is not generally observed, except by Philo.
